WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Newton’s first law says an object stays at rest or continues at constant velocity unless a net external force acts on it.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Newton’s second law states that net force equals mass multiplied by acceleration. We write this as F equals m times a.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:28.000
A six newton net force on a two kilogram cart produces an acceleration of three metres per second squared.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Action and reaction forces have equal magnitude and opposite directions, but they act on different objects.
